@page "/features"
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>Features | BloodLink</PageTitle>
<PublicSite>
<main id="main-content" class="public-features">
    <header class="bl-container public-features-intro"><span class="public-kicker">The BloodLink workspace</span><h1>Practical tools.<br />Connected work.</h1><p class="public-lead">From the stock on your shelves to the request in your inbox, keep the information your team needs within reach.</p><div class="public-feature-index"><span>01 Inventory</span><span>02 Needs &amp; requests</span><span>03 Facility operations</span><span>04 Accountability</span><span>05 Access</span></div></header>
    <section class="public-feature-family bl-container" aria-labelledby="inventory-title"><div class="public-family-copy"><span class="public-kicker">01 / Inventory management</span><h2 id="inventory-title">A clear view of what is available.</h2><p>Stock visibility starts with quantities that mean something to the team making the next decision.</p><ul><li>Current inventory by blood type</li><li>Available and reserved units shown separately</li><li>Inventory adjustments with a recorded reason</li><li>Transaction history for stock changes</li></ul></div><figure class="public-product-frame"><div class="public-window-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>Inventory</span></div><img src="images/product-inventory.webp" width="1440" height="948" loading="lazy" alt="Actual BloodLink inventory screen showing blood types and total, reserved and available units with demonstration data" /><figcaption>Actual interface · demonstration data</figcaption></figure></section>
    <div class="public-family-tint"><section class="public-feature-family public-family-reverse bl-container" aria-labelledby="requests-title"><div class="public-family-copy"><span class="public-kicker">02 / Needs &amp; requests</span><h2 id="requests-title">Keep the request moving, with context.</h2><p>A recorded need connects to an availability search and a facility-to-facility request.</p><ul><li>Create and review blood needs</li><li>Search availability across facilities</li><li>Follow requests sent and received</li><li>Accept, reject and confirm handover</li></ul></div><figure class="public-product-frame"><div class="public-window-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>Requests received</span></div><img src="images/product-requests-received.webp" width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy" alt="Actual BloodLink requests received screen showing a request's facility, blood type, quantity and status with demonstration data" /><figcaption>Actual interface · demonstration data</figcaption></figure></section></div>
    <section class="public-feature-family bl-container" aria-labelledby="operations-title"><div class="public-family-copy"><span class="public-kicker">03 / Facility operations</span><h2 id="operations-title">A workspace for your team.</h2><p>Facility administrators keep the profile current and manage staff access from the same workspace.</p><ul><li>Facility profile and contact information</li><li>Create and manage facility staff accounts</li><li>Responsibilities defined by role</li></ul></div><figure class="public-product-frame"><div class="public-window-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>Facility staff</span></div><img src="images/product-facility-staff.webp" width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy" alt="Actual BloodLink staff management screen displaying demonstration team members and account statuses" /><figcaption>Actual interface · demonstration data</figcaption></figure></section>
    <div class="public-family-tint"><section class="public-feature-family public-family-reverse bl-container" aria-labelledby="accountability-title"><div class="public-family-copy"><span class="public-kicker">04 / Visibility &amp; accountability</span><h2 id="accountability-title">The record stays with the work.</h2><p>Keep request updates and stock changes visible beyond the moment they happen.</p><ul><li>Notifications linked to relevant records</li><li>Need and request status history</li><li>Facility activity with recorded actors and times</li><li>Inventory transaction records</li></ul></div><figure class="public-product-frame"><div class="public-window-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>Activity</span></div><img src="images/product-activity.webp" width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy" alt="Actual BloodLink activity history showing recorded actions, actors and timestamps with demonstration data" /><figcaption>Actual interface · demonstration data</figcaption></figure></section></div>
    <section class="public-section bl-container public-security-family" aria-labelledby="security-title"><div><span class="public-kicker">05 / Administration &amp; security</span><h2 id="security-title">Access follows responsibility.</h2><p>Staff, facility administrators and system administrators have distinct responsibilities in BloodLink.</p></div><div class="public-access-composition"><AppIcon Name="shield" Size="38" /><h3>Controlled facility access</h3><dl><div><dt>Staff</dt><dd>Inventory visibility and their own needs</dd></div><div><dt>Facility administrators</dt><dd>Facility operations and coordination</dd></div><div><dt>System administrators</dt><dd>Facility governance and access controls</dd></div></dl></div></section>
    <section class="public-final-cta bl-container"><h2>Put these tools to work for your facility.</h2><div class="bl-action-row"><a class="bl-btn bl-btn-primary bl-btn-lg" href="/facility/register">Register facility</a><a class="bl-btn bl-btn-outline bl-btn-lg" href="/how-it-works">Follow the workflow</a></div></section>
</main>
</PublicSite>
